# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backend/.env holds MONGO_URL, JWT_SECRET, ADMIN_PASSWORD and the EMERGENT_*
# API keys. It must never be committed — hosting platforms inject these as
# environment variables, and python-dotenv leaves already-set vars alone, so no
# file is needed in production. See backend/.env.example for the shape.
backend/.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

# frontend/.env is deliberately NOT ignored: it carries only REACT_APP_* values,
# which are compiled into the public bundle by design, and the Pages build reads
# it. Never put a secret there — anything REACT_APP_* is world-readable.
